1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
We sit for hours and slowly creep toward the screen —
head forward, shoulders tight — and never notice until it hurts.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Nunchikochi is a calm desk coach that reads posture and
fatigue cues from your webcam — never who you are.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
It never keeps the frames, and nudges you only when it matters.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Here's the whole app. One promise up front:
each frame is analysed in memory on AWS and discarded immediately.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Never recorded, never stored.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Only aggregate numbers — counts and seconds — are kept
for your daily report.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
It's a wellbeing nudge, not a diagnosis.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Pick Live mode, allow the camera,
and it spends five seconds learning your neutral posture.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Then it runs. Turn on "what OpenCV sees" and you get
the face box and landmark points — coordinates only, no image leaves the view.

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Lean in and hold it, and a gentle nudge appears: sit back a little.

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Two at most, so it never buries the live metrics.

12
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Under the overlay, OpenCV 5 runs the whole vision path:
it detects the face and finds landmarks.

13
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:24,000
It derives the signals — eye-openness, head tilt,
and how close you are.

14
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:40,000
It also scores image quality, and when quality is poor
it can take a second look before anyone is bothered.

15
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:54,000
This is the Agentic Vision part. The coach doesn't act on a single frame.

16
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:08,000
When it's uncertain, it asks OpenCV to look again —
and that result changes the plan.

17
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:22,000
If the second look clears things up, it stays quiet.
If it's still unsure, it asks you a yes or no.

18
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:30,000
You're always in control. Anything off-list the model suggests
is rejected, and the rules decide instead.

19
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:43,000
It runs on AWS: OpenCV 5 inside a single Lambda on arm64 Graviton,
with a hard concurrency cap of five.

20
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Session state lives in DynamoDB with a 24-hour expiry,
and frames are never written to disk, S3, or logs.

21
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:06,000
We don't hide the limits. The agent passes twenty-two deterministic
scenarios and nine adversarial ones.

22
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:14,000
We left one failing on purpose — the bug was in the test, not the agent.

23
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Watch a real failure path: in a dark room the quality warning fires,
the second look doesn't clear it, so instead of guessing it asks you.

24
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Nunchikochi — OpenCV 5 that sees, an agent that decides with you,
on AWS, with your frames never kept. Thanks for watching.
